start-stop-discontinue type is used to specify ending types. Typically, the start type is associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a downward","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is typical for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second endings that do not conclude a piece."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"}}}